@* Present so the Razor SDK treats this project as hosting Blazor components.

   The components themselves live in Tamp.Findings.Web (ADR 0002). But the SDK
   decides whether to bring in the framework's static web assets — the package
   that carries blazor.web.js — by looking for Razor items in the HOST project,
   not in a referenced RCL. Without any, MapStaticAssets has nothing to serve
   and /_framework/blazor.web.js 404s, so no circuit ever boots.
*@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
